      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes perfect sense that longing for wholeness creates an impossible expectation; no amount of pretending can fill a void left by someone who cannot be replaced by others. While the pain makes life feel pointless, remember that staying and slowly rebuilding those pieces is what allows a new version of \"you\" to emerge, distinct from the past. Please consider reaching out to a therapist once today, not as a burden for others, but as an act of kindness toward the only life this exhausted half can offer itself.",
